 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? A sketch is quick, rough idea, often only one character or setting, whereas a study is usually more detailed, with multiple characters and more action. Kind of. Sketches often form the basis of a full drawing or painting later, so they' a great way to warm up. A lovely project. For the landscape, start with skitches. The big picture. How far away you want it, what's in the foreground, what's in the sky. Get those big shapes down first, then worry about the finer details. Enjoy it. It's a nice break before the main event.",
